From 1b7ed79533e9dc746b65091b5caebabf2b0a5abd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marc Lainez <marc.lainez@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Mar 2026 19:40:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 07/11] power: supply: qcom_pmi632_qg: fix current_now sign
 convention

The PMI632 QG hardware reports current with positive values for
discharge and negative for charge. The power_supply sysfs ABI
(Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-class-power) specifies the opposite:
positive for charging, negative for discharging.

Negate the raw reading to match the ABI, so that current_now is
positive when the battery is charging and status reports Charging.

Signed-off-by: Marc Lainez <marc.lainez@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom_pmi632_qg.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_pmi632_qg.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_pmi632_qg.c
index faca46c8b..f300380bf 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_pmi632_qg.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_pmi632_qg.c
@@ -198,7 +198,12 @@ static int qg_read_ibat(struct pmi632_qg *qg, int *ibat_ua)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	*ibat_ua = QG_I_RAW_TO_UA(sign_extend32(raw, 15));
+	/*
+	 * Hardware convention: positive = discharge, negative = charge.
+	 * Power supply class convention (ABI): positive = charge, negative = discharge.
+	 * Negate to match the ABI.
+	 */
+	*ibat_ua = -QG_I_RAW_TO_UA(sign_extend32(raw, 15));
 	return 0;
 }
 
